{"title":"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 40","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_40&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the number of integers n that satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/4/814e2f3cef9d8435f274babfda765730b332fd07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{both}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> of the following conditions:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/1/fc13a4042b7f9b39a9941b54c33c49cb68541167.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$208&lt;n&lt;2008$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"122\" height=\"13\" />,\nn has the same remainder when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> or by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_40&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, find which numbers have the same remainder when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> or by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.  With some experimentation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be congruent to numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/0/6506f8a3fc12c35809acdfd50e1c0f1a1a34e8a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 120k + m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"110\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/4/9b48bb414195ae3a60d955cdbc613599f215ae14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le m \\le 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/8/9c85284a3ada685512410cc9e0f69108d745150e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\le k \\le 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> will result in an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2e1ede8a74738aac472b16f350cd78df611e9dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$208 &lt; n &lt; 2008$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"122\" height=\"13\" />.  Additionally, when checking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fab47c0b9d0ce398d03e57d6720129d53434f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/0/b50b9ef50569e82e43aef780e6d2a0bca97a20ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 23$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, no values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> satisfies the boundaries.  Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/9/5d9ccad7139c5390007824335a74795495ac87fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 \\cdot 24 = \\boxed{360}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" /> integers that satisfy both conditions.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_40&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest\" title=\"2008 iTest\">2008 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align